{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"BLOCKER: epic 759e-7dc1-675c-4877's plan-review PASSes content review (0 blocking findings after 2 remediation rounds — same content as the already-certified children) but sign fails with a reproducible 'stale-head' error whose reported 'current HEAD' (f1dd41a8f09967dd60c7aefb5e43c6f62fa119af, an unrelated commit titled 'Diagnose MCP client PAT wiring in doctor') does not match origin/main, gerrit/main, or this worktree's own HEAD (9a94ef9737fb, confirmed stable via reflog). The value was IDENTICAL across 2 independent review runs ~15min apart, ruling out ordinary live contention. Filed as bug seaworthy-revengeful-blobfish (discovered_from this epic) with full investigation trail. This blocks claim of the epic directly and via the parent-claim cascade for every child (confirmed: attempting to claim celestine-treasonous-ewe, already certified itself, fails because its open parent cannot be claimed). Cannot use --force per AGENTS.md agent policy. Running one more diagnostic retry (review-epic4.log) to see if the bogus HEAD value ever changes (would indicate contention rather than a stuck bug) before deciding whether to escalate to the user as fully blocked.\n\nProgress so far: undamaged-adept-xenarthra (usage_log bug) and celestine-treasonous-ewe (corpus builder) both certified after real remediation of genuine blocking findings (fingerprint generation-ladder correctness mirroring attest._legacy_material_ok exactly, manifest determinism via sorted-key serialization, multi-ticket-id ambiguity resolved to first-element rule, a missed third call site)."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788037709537622386,"uuid":"fd6870f5-b9e2-4bfe-81f9-810e